# The e2e fixture's copy of the addon. Generated, not authored: scripts/test-gd.ps1,
# CI and the e2e suite each mirror addons/godot_mcp over it before running. Tracking
# it meant every addon change had to be duplicated by hand or the committed copy went
# stale — pure diff noise, and a stale copy silently tests the wrong code.
mcp-server/src/tests/fixtures/e2e-project/addons/godot_mcp/

# Internal planning and research: audits, competitive analysis, roadmaps.
# Kept in the working tree so they live next to the code they describe, but never
# committed — this repo is public. Nothing here has ever been in a commit, which
# is the point: on a public repo, deleting a branch or force-pushing does NOT
# remove the objects (they stay reachable by SHA through the fork network), so
# "commit now, hide later" is not an option. See notes/LONGTERM.md.
notes/
